      "name": "Grid Certification of the ε-Interleaving Relation",
      "description": "Decides, on a finite sample of scales, whether two Vietoris-Rips persistence modules M = RipsMod d and N = RipsMod d' are eps-interleaved, i.e. whether M(t) <= N(t+eps) and N(t) <= M(t+eps) for all sampled t. Each test is an edge-set inclusion in the lattice Set(X x X). For n points and S sampled scales the cost is O(S * n^2) set-membership checks; correctness on the continuum follows because both obj maps are step functions with breakpoints at the finite set of pairwise dissimilarity values, so it suffices to test scales straddling those breakpoints. This algorithm is the computational shadow of the relation `Interleaved` and the building block for the interleaving-distance search.",
      "pseudocode": "function IS_INTERLEAVED(d, d', points, eps, scales):\n  for t in scales:\n    A  <- { (x,y) : d (x,y)  <= t       }\n    B  <- { (x,y) : d'(x,y)  <= t + eps  }\n    C  <- { (x,y) : d'(x,y)  <= t       }\n    D  <- { (x,y) : d (x,y)  <= t + eps  }\n    if not (A subset B) or not (C subset D):\n      return False\n  return True",
