      "description": "Computes interleavingDist(RipsMod d, RipsMod d') = inf { eps >= 0 : eps-interleaved }. Because the interleaving predicate is monotone in eps (weakening: more slack never hurts), the admissible set is an up-set, so the infimum is found by scanning an increasing grid and returning the first eps that certifies interleaving; a binary search over the grid sharpens this to O(log(1/h)) interleaving tests of cost O(S*n^2) each. The output is an upper estimate of the true infimum, tightening as the grid step h -> 0. This realizes the verified bound interleavingDist <= ENNReal.ofReal(||d - d'||_inf).",
      "pseudocode": "function INTERLEAVING_DISTANCE(d, d', points, eps_grid, scales):\n  sort eps_grid ascending\n  lo, hi <- 0, len(eps_grid) - 1\n  # monotone predicate: binary search for first True\n  if not IS_INTERLEAVED(d, d', points, eps_grid[hi], scales):\n      return +infinity\n  while lo < hi:\n      mid <- (lo + hi) // 2\n      if IS_INTERLEAVED(d, d', points, eps_grid[mid], scales):\n          hi <- mid\n      else:\n          lo <- mid + 1\n  return eps_grid[lo]",
      "code": "from typing import Dict, List, Tuple\n\nEdge = Tuple[int, int]\nDissimilarity = Dict[Edge, float]\n\ndef interleaving_distance(d: Dissimilarity, d2: Dissimilarity,\n                          points: List[int], eps_grid: List[float],\n                          scales: List[float]) -> float:\n    grid = sorted(eps_grid)\n    if not grid or not is_interleaved(d, d2, points, grid[-1], scales):\n        return float('inf')\n    lo, hi = 0, len(grid) - 1\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if is_interleaved(d, d2, points, grid[mid], scales):\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    return grid[lo]\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tropical Composition of Interleaving Certificates",
      "description": "Implements the composition law Interleaved.trans: given an eps-interleaving certificate for (M, N) and a delta-interleaving certificate for (N, L), it returns an (eps+delta)-interleaving certificate for (M, L). The shift combines under tropical MULTIPLICATION, eps (x)_trop delta = eps + delta, while the optimal distance combines under tropical ADDITION (minimum). The routine therefore both produces the composite certificate and reports the tropical product of the two shifts, witnessing the triangle inequality interleavingDist(M,L) <= interleavingDist(M,N) + interleavingDist(N,L) as min-plus submultiplicativity. Cost is O(1) beyond the verification of the composite shift.",
      "pseudocode": "function TROPICAL_COMPOSE(eps, delta):\n  # tropical multiplication of interleaving shifts\n  composite_shift <- eps + delta        # (x)_trop\n  return composite_shift\n\nfunction TROPICAL_BEST(d1, d2):\n  # tropical addition selects the better (smaller) shift\n  return min(d1, d2)                     # (+)_trop",
      "code": "def trop_mul(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Tropical multiplication = ordinary addition (shifts compose).\"\"\"\n    return a + b\n\ndef trop_add(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Tropical addition = minimum (optimal interleaving).\"\"\"\n    return min(a, b)\n\ndef tropical_compose(eps: float, delta: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Compose an eps- and a delta-interleaving: shift = eps (x)_trop delta.\"\"\"\n    assert eps >= 0 and delta >= 0\n    return trop_mul(eps, delta)\n"
    }
